---
// Core page (maximum-gain). Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-hdb-approved.json (2026-07-13).
// Rule facts verbatim from hdb.gov.sg (crawled 2026-07-13, list updated 6 May 2026).
// Licence-transfer evidence owner-confirmed 2026-07-13.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PawTrail from '../components/PawTrail.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../assets/site/12-maltipoo-hdb-living-room.webp';

const title = 'Are Maltipoos HDB Approved? Yes, By Rule | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Maltipoos are HDB approved by rule: Maltese (item 33), Toy Poodle (item 42) and item 62 approve the cross. The proof from HDB’s own list, plus licence steps.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'HDB Guide', url: '/maltipoo-hdb-approved' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Is a Maltipoo an HDB approved breed?',
    a: 'Yes, by rule rather than by grace. HDB’s approved list names the Maltese at item 33 and the Toy and Miniature Poodle at item 42, and item 62 approves a cross of any two breeds in items 1 to 61. A Maltipoo is exactly that cross, so it qualifies outright.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which crossbreeds are HDB approved?',
    a: 'Any cross of two breeds that both appear in items 1 to 61 of the HDB list. That covers the Maltipoo (Maltese x Toy Poodle) and equivalents like the Cavapoo (Cavalier King Charles Spaniel x Poodle). A cross involving a breed NOT on the list does not inherit approval.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I keep two Maltipoos in an HDB flat?',
    a: 'No. HDB allows one dog from the approved list per flat, and flat owners found breaching the rule can be fined up to $4,000. If your household wants two dogs, that usually means one registered at another eligible address, or private property.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I keep a Maltipoo and cats together in a flat?',
    a: 'Yes. Since 1 September 2024, HDB allows up to two licensed cats as well as one dog of an approved breed in the same flat. Both species need their own AVS licences.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do condos follow the same approved list?',
    a: 'No, the list is an HDB rule. Condominiums set their own by-laws through the MCST, and most allow small dogs like a 2 to 4kg Maltipoo, but check your estate’s rules before buying rather than after.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What licence does my Maltipoo need, and when?',
    a: 'Every dog in Singapore must hold an AVS licence through the PALS system, HDB flat or not. We complete the paperwork with you at purchase, and your first year costs $13.50 because a nine-week-old puppy is under the five-month fee threshold.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/maltipoo-hdb-approved',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'HDB approval for Maltipoos',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/maltipoo-hdb-approved" schemas={schemas}>
  <section class="container-site pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12 relative overflow-hidden rise-in">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="absolute -top-8 -right-8 w-44 h-44 text-white/40" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute top-6 right-[22%] w-9 h-9 text-primary/25 float-soft" style="--float-rot: 14deg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute bottom-5 right-[10%] w-7 h-7 text-primary/20 float-soft" style="--float-rot: -10deg; animation-delay: -2.6s" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute -bottom-10 -left-10 w-40 h-40 text-primary/8" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <div class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 opacity-30"><PawTrail /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative">
      <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">HDB guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">Are Maltipoos HDB approved?</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[52ch] mb-5">
        "Is Maltipoo HDB approved" is the question every flat-dwelling buyer types before
        falling for a face. Plenty of listings stamp "HDB Approved!" on a photo; here is the
        actual rule, from the HDB approved breeds list itself, plus everything that comes with
        the yes.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! I live in an HDB flat and would like to ask about Maltipoo puppies.')} class="btn-cta">Ask about HDB-ready puppies</a>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="Is a Maltipoo HDB approved?">
    Yes, by rule. HDB's approved-breeds list names the Maltese at item 33 and the Toy and
    Miniature Poodle at item 42, and item 62 approves "a cross of any 2 breeds in items 1 to
    61": a cross of two approved breeds is itself approved, which is exactly what a Maltipoo
    is. You may keep one dog per flat from the approved list, and every dog needs an AVS
    licence.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <section class="container-site pt-8">
    <img
      src={featuredImg.src}
      width={featuredImg.width}
      height={featuredImg.height}
      alt="Apricot Maltipoo resting in a playpen corner of an HDB flat living room"
      loading="lazy"
      class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]"
    />
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The proof, from HDB's own list" id="proof">
    <p>
      Open HDB's
      <a href="https://www.hdb.gov.sg/managing-my-home/home-ownership/keeping-pets" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Guidelines on Keeping Pets</a>
      and count down the approved list. Item 33 is the Maltese. Item 42 is the Poodle, toy or
      miniature. Then item 62 closes the question: "Cross of any 2 breeds in items 1 to 61."
    </p>
    <p>
      A Maltipoo is a Maltese crossed with a Toy or Miniature Poodle, both named on the list,
      so the cross is approved by the list itself, not by a seller's badge. The page was last
      updated in May 2026, and it is the only source that matters on this question.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The three-line proof"
      items={[
        'Item 33: Maltese, named on the HDB list',
        'Item 42: Poodle (Toy or Miniature), named',
        'Item 62: cross of any 2 breeds in items 1 to 61',
        'Maltese x Toy Poodle = Maltipoo = approved',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Why some sites still call crossbreeds a grey area" id="grey-area" reverse>
    <p>
      You will find breed guides claiming crossbreeds are "not officially HDB-approved under
      the standard list." Read item 62 again; the list approves crosses explicitly. The grey
      area framing survives because few writers scroll past item 61, and because "check with
      HDB" is a safer sentence than a citation.
    </p>
    <p>
      We can add operational proof to the paper one. When a shop transfers an AVS dog licence
      to a customer, the system flags any breed that needs separate HDB approval for a flat.
      Across {site.maltipoosPlaced} Maltipoo placements, many into HDB homes, that flag has
      never appeared for a Maltipoo. A note from the shop floor: the transfer screen is the
      moment a wrong breed claim would surface, and it never has.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Rule + reality"
      items={[
        'The rule: item 62 approves the cross',
        'The reality: 100+ licence transfers, zero flags',
        'The badge on a listing proves neither',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The rules that come with the yes" id="rules" tinted>
    <p>
      HDB approval is a package, not a blank cheque. The full list of HDB approved dogs runs
      to 62 items, all small companion sizes, and you may keep one dog per flat, with fines up
      to $4,000 for breaches. Every dog must be licensed with AVS through PALS,
      per the
      <a href="https://avs.nparks.gov.sg/pets/licensing-a-pet/information-on-dog-and-cat-licences/licensing-requirements/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">licensing requirements</a>:
      $13.50 a year under five months, $81 a year unsterilised after that, and $13.50 a year or
      a one-time $35 lifetime licence once sterilised.
    </p>
    <p>
      The rule HDB spells out beyond paperwork is consideration: care for your dog so it does
      not bark continuously, and keep it inside the flat. With a vocal, people-attached breed
      like the Maltipoo, that means teaching quiet and settled-alone habits from week one,
      which is exactly what the included trainer lesson starts on.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="HDB dog rules, complete"
      items={[
        'One approved-list dog per flat',
        'Fine up to $4,000 for breaches',
        'AVS licence mandatory (PALS)',
        'Fees: $13.50 under 5 months; $81 unsterilised; $35 lifetime sterilised',
        'Up to 2 licensed cats may share the flat',
        'No continuous barking; dog stays within the flat',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Why a toy Maltipoo fits flat life beyond the rulebook" id="flat-life">
    <p>
      Approval says a Maltipoo may live in a flat; a 2 to 4kg frame says it lives there
      comfortably. Fifteen to twenty minutes of morning walk before the heat, indoor play in
      the evening, and a lap for the hours between covers its needs, and the featherweight
      build makes lifts, void decks and carriers easy.
    </p>
    <p>
      The honest caveat is company, not space. A Maltipoo wants someone around through the day,
      so run the <a href="/#lifestyle-fit">routine check</a> before you fall for a face. If
      your flat is empty from 8am to 6pm, we will point you to a more independent breed and
      mean it.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Flat-fit, honestly"
      items={[
        'Space: featherweight, any flat size works',
        'Exercise: short walks, indoor play',
        'Noise: vocal breed, train quiet early',
        'Company: wants someone home most days',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="How we handle licensing when you buy" id="licensing" reverse>
    <p>
      At purchase we complete the AVS licence paperwork with you, so your Maltipoo goes home
      already licensed to your name and address. The first year costs $13.50, because a
      nine-week-old puppy sits under the five-month threshold, and the fee is folded into the
      <a href="/maltipoo-price-singapore">all-in price</a> workflow rather than left as
      homework.
    </p>
    <p>
      First dog in the household? Singapore asks first-time owners to complete the free online
      <a href="https://avs.nparks.gov.sg/pets/licensing-a-pet/applying-for-dog-and-cat-licences/pet-ownership-course/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">AVS Pet Ownership Course</a>
      before licensing. We point you to it during purchase so it never delays the homecoming.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Licensing, handled"
      items={[
        'Paperwork completed with you at purchase',
        'First licence: $13.50 for the year',
        'Course link provided for first-timers',
        'Renewal reminders from us, not fines from AVS',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="The yes is settled"
    secondaryText="See the apricot toy Maltipoos currently available, all HDB-ready by rule."
    secondaryHref="/puppies"
    secondaryLabel="See available puppies"
  />
</BaseLayout>
